(window.MAG=window.MAG||{}).d=(window.MAG.d||{});window.MAG.d["2-lateran-iii"]=[["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p1","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","Although concerning the avoidance of discord in the election of the supreme pontiff, sufficiently clear [decrees] have issued forth from our predecessors, nevertheless because after those [decrees] the church has often suffered grievous division through the audacity of depraved ambition, we also, for the purpose of avoiding this evil, have decreed something to be added by the counsel of our brothers and by the approval of the sacred council.","Licet de evitanda discordia in electione summi pontificis manifesta satis a nostris praedecessoribus constituta manaverint tamen quia saepe post illa per improbae ambitionis audaciam gravem passa est ecclesia scissuram nos etiam ad malum hoc evitandum de consilio fratrum nostrorum et sacri approbatione concilii aliquid decrevimus adiungendum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p2","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","We decree therefore that if by chance, the enemy of mankind oversowing tares, full agreement concerning installing a pontiff shall not have been able to be had among the cardinals, and with two parts agreeing, the third part shall have been unwilling to agree or shall have presumed to ordain another for itself, let him be held as Roman pontiff who shall have been elected and received by the two parts.","Statuimus igitur ut si forte inimico homine superseminante zizania inter cardinales de substituendo pontifice non potuerit concordia plena esse et duabus partibus concordantibus tertia pars noluerit concordare aut sibi alium praesumpserit ordinare ille Romanus pontifex habeatur qui a duabus partibus fuerit electus et receptus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p3","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","But if anyone, relying upon the nomination of the third part because he cannot obtain the reality, shall have usurped the name of bishop, let both he himself and those who shall have received him be subject to excommunication and be punished with the deprivation of every sacred order, so that even viaticum be denied to them except only in their last moments, and unless they shall have repented, let them receive a portion with Dathan and Abiram whom the earth swallowed alive.","Si quis autem de tertiae partis nominatione confisus quia rem non potest sibi nomen episcopi usurpaverit tam ipse quam qui eum receperint excommunicationi subiaceant et totius sacri ordinis privatione mulctentur ita ut viatici eis etiam nisi tantum in ultimis communio denegetur et nisi resipuerint cum Dathan et Abiron quos terra vivos absorbuit accipiant portionem."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p4","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","Moreover, if anyone shall have been elected to the office of apostle by fewer than the two parts, unless greater agreement shall have intervened, let him by no means be assumed, and let him be subject to the aforesaid penalty if he shall have been unwilling humbly to abstain.","Praeterea si a paucioribus aliquis quam a duabus partibus fuerit electus ad apostolatus officium nisi maior concordia intercesserit nullatenus assumatur et praedictae poenae subiaceat si humiliter noluerit abstinere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p5","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","From this, however, let no prejudice be generated to canonical constitutions and other ecclesiastical [regulations] in which the sentence of the greater and senior part ought to prevail, because what shall have come into doubt in them can be defined by the judgment of a superior.","Ex hoc tamen nullum canonicis constitutionibus et aliis ecclesiasticis praeiudicium generetur in quibus maioris et senioris partis debet sententia praevalere quia quod in eis dubium venerit superioris poterit iudicio definiri."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p6","Third Lateran Council A.d. 1179","But in the Roman church something special is established because recourse to a superior cannot be had.","In Romana vero ecclesia aliquid speciale constituitur quia non potest recursus ad superiorem haberi."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p7","Canon II","Renewing what was done by our predecessor of happy memory Innocent, we judge that the ordinations made by the haeresiarchae Octavian and Guido and also by John of Struma who followed them, and those made by those ordained by them, are invalid, adding also that if any persons have received ecclesiastical dignities or benefices through the aforesaid schismatics, they shall lack what they have obtained.","Quod a praedecessore nostro felicis memoriae Innocentio factum est innovantes ordinationes ab Octaviano et Guidone haeresiarchis necnon et Iohanne Strumensi qui eos secutus est factas et ab ordinatis ab eis irritas esse censemus adicientes etiam ut si qui dignitates ecclesiasticas seu beneficia per praedictos schismaticos receperunt careant impetratis."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p8","Canon II","Also alienations or invasions which have been made by the same schismatics or by laypersons concerning ecclesiastical affairs, let them lack all firmness and let them revert to the church without any burden upon it.","Alienationes quoque seu invasiones quae per eosdem schismaticos sive per laicos factae sunt de rebus ecclesiasticis omni careant firmitate et ad ecclesiam sine omni eius onere revertantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p9","Canon II","But if anyone shall have presumed to act against this, let him know that he lies under excommunication.","Si quis autem contraire praesumpserit excommunicationi se noverit subiacere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p10","Canon II","Those moreover who voluntarily have sworn an oath of maintaining the schism we have decreed to remain suspended from sacred orders and dignities.","Illos autem qui sponte iuramentum de tenendo schismate praestiterint a sacris ordinibus et dignitatibus decrevimus manere suspensos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p11","Canon III","Since in sacred orders and ecclesiastical ministries both maturity of age and gravity of morals and knowledge of letters must be sought, much more strongly it is fitting that these things be sought in a bishop who, placed in the care of others, ought to show in himself how others ought to conduct themselves in the house of the Lord.","Cum in sacris ordinibus et ministeriis ecclesiasticis et aetatis maturitas et morum gravitas et scientia litterarum sit inquirenda multo fortius haec in episcopo oportet inquiri qui ad curam positus aliorum in se ipso debet ostendere qualiter alios in domo domini oporteat conversari."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p12","Canon III","Therefore, lest what has been done concerning certain persons out of necessity of time be drawn into an example by posterity, by the present decree we decree that no one be elected as bishop unless he shall have already completed the thirtieth year of his age and has been born of legitimate marriage, who also is shown to be commendable in life and knowledge.","Eapropter ne quod de quibusdam ex necessitate temporis factum est in exemplum trahatur a posteris praesenti decreto statuimus ut nullus in episcopum eligatur nisi qui iam trigesimum aetatis annum egerit et de legitimo sit matrimonio natus qui etiam vita et scientia commendabilis demonstretur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p13","Canon III","But when he shall have been elected and shall have received confirmation of the election and shall have had the administration of ecclesiastical goods, the time defined by the canons concerning consecrating bishops having elapsed, let him to whom the benefices which he had pertained have free faculty of disposing concerning them.","Cum autem electus fuerit et confirmationem electionis acceperit et ecclesiasticorum bonorum administrationem habuerit decurso tempore de consecrandis episcopis a canonibus definito is ad quem spectant beneficia quae habuerat disponendi de illis liberam habeat facultatem."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p14","Canon IV","Let no one at all receive inferior ministries—for example, deaneries, archdeaconries, and other things which have the care of souls annexed—nor even the governance of parochial churches unless he shall have already attained the twenty-fifth year of his age and who exists as commendable in knowledge and morals.","Inferiora etiam ministeria utputa decanatus archidiaconatus et alia quae animarum curam habent annexam nullus omnino suscipiat sed nec parochialium ecclesiarum regimen nisi qui iam vigesimum quintum aetatis annum attigerit et qui scientia et moribus exsistat commendandus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p15","Canon IV","But when he shall have been assumed, if an archdeacon shall not have been ordained a deacon, and deans and the rest, having been admonished within the time fixed by the canons, shall not have been ordained as presbyters, let them also be removed from that office and let it be conferred upon another who is both willing and able to fulfill it suitably.","Cum autem assumptus fuerit si archidiaconus in diaconum et decani et reliqui admoniti non fuerint praefixo a canonibus tempore in presbyteros ordinati et ab illo removeantur officio et alii conferatur qui et velit et possit convenienter illud implere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p16","Canon IV","Nor let the refuge of appeal profit them if by chance they shall have wished to protect themselves by appeal in transgression of this constitution.","Nec prosit illis appellationis diffugium si forte in transgressionem constitutionis istius per appellationem voluerint se tueri."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p17","Canon IV","This we command to be observed not only concerning those to be promoted but also concerning those already promoted, if the canons do not stand against it.","Hoc sane non solum de promovendis sed de his etiam qui iam promoti sunt si canones non obsistant praecipimus observandum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p18","Canon V","Clearly, if clerics shall have elected anyone against this form, let them know that they are then deprived of the power of electing and suspended from ecclesiastical benefices for three years.","Clerici sane si contra formam istam quemquam elegerint et eligendi potestate tunc privatos et ab ecclesiasticis beneficiis triennio se noverint suspensos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p19","Canon V","For it is worthy that those whom the fear of God does not recall from evil, at least the severity of ecclesiastical discipline coerce.","Dignum est enim ut quos timor dei a malo non revocat ecclesiasticae saltem coerceat severitas disciplinae."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p20","Canon V","But if a bishop shall have done or consented to be done against this concerning conferring the aforesaid things, let him lose his power.","Episcopus autem si cui fecerit aut fieri consenserit contra hoc in conferendis praedictis potestatem suam amittat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p21","Canon V","And let them be ordained by the chapter or by the metropolitan if the chapter shall have been unable to agree.","Et per capitulum aut per metropolitanum si capitulum concordare nequiverit ordinentur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p22","Canon VI","Since the apostle decreed that he and his own should be supported by their own hands, so that he might take away the place of preaching from pseudo-apostles and might not be burdensome to those to whom he preached, it is recognized as too grave and worthy of correction that some of our brothers and fellow bishops are so heavy upon their subjects in their procurations that for this cause subjects are sometimes compelled to pawn ecclesiastical ornaments and a brief hour consumes the provisions of a long time.","Cum apostolus se et suos propriis manibus decreverit exhibendos ut locum praedicandi auferret pseudoapostolis et illis quibus praedicabat non exsisteret onerosus grave nimis et emendatione fore dignum dignoscitur quod quidam fratrum et coepiscoporum nostrorum ita graves in procurationibus suis subditis exsistant ut pro huiusmodi causa interdum ornamenta ecclesiastica subditi compellantur exponere et longi temporis victum brevis hora consumat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p23","Canon VI","Wherefore, we decree that archbishops visiting parishes, according to the diversity of provinces and the resources of churches, shall not exceed the number of forty or fifty horses.","Quocirca statuimus quod archiepiscopi parochias visitantes pro diversitate provinciarum et facultatibus ecclesiarum quadraginta vel quinquaginta evectionis numerum non excedant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p24","Canon VI","But cardinals shall not exceed twenty or twenty-five; bishops shall by no means exceed twenty or thirty; archdeacons shall be content with five or seven; deans constituted under them with two horses.","Cardinales vero viginti vel viginti quinque non excedant episcopi viginti vel triginta nequaquam excedant archidiaconi quinque aut septem decani constituti sub ipsis duobus equis exsistant contenti."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p25","Canon VI","Nor let them set out with hunting dogs and birds, but let them proceed so that they may seem to seek not their own things but those of Jesus Christ.","Nec cum canibus venatoriis et avibus proficiscantur sed ita procedant ut non quae sunt sua sed quae Iesu Christi quaerere videantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p26","Canon VI","Nor let them seek sumptuous feasts, but with thanksgiving let them receive what shall have been ministered to them honorably and suitably.","Nec sumptuosas epulas quaerant sed cum gratiarum actione recipiant quod honeste et competenter fuerit illis ministratum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p27","Canon VI","We also forbid that bishops presume to burden their subjects with tolls and exactions.","Prohibemus etiam ne subditos suos talliis et exactionibus episcopi gravare praesumant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p28","Canon VI","We endure, however, on account of the many necessities which sometimes arise, that if a manifest and reasonable cause shall have existed, they may be able to seek moderate aid from them with charity.","Sustinemus autem pro multis necessitatibus quae aliquoties superveniunt ut si manifesta et rationabilis causa exstiterit cum caritate moderatum ab eis valeant auxilium postulare."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p29","Canon VI","For since the apostle says \"Children ought not to lay up treasure for their parents but parents for children,\" it seems very far from paternal piety if prelates are heavy upon their subjects whom they ought in the manner of a shepherd to support in all necessities.","Cum enim dicat apostolus non debent parentibus filii thesaurizare sed parentes filiis multum longe a paterna pietate videtur si praepositi suis subditis graves exsistant quos in cunctis necessitatibus pastoris more fovere debent."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p30","Canon VI","Moreover, archdeacons or deans shall not presume to exercise any exactions or tolls upon presbyters or clerics.","Archidiaconi autem sive decani nullas exactiones vel tallias in presbyteros seu clericos exercere praesumant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p31","Canon VII","Clearly, what has been said concerning the aforesaid number of horses according to tolerance is able to be observed in those places in which incomes and the resources of churches are more ample.","Sane quod de praedicto numero evectionis secundum tolerantiam dictum est in illis locis poterit observari in quibus ampliores sunt reditus et ecclesiae facultates."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p32","Canon VII","But in poorer places we wish such a measure to be held that from the arrival of greater persons lesser ones ought not to be burdened, lest under such indulgence those who have been accustomed to use fewer horses up to now believe that very ample power has been granted to them.","In pauperioribus autem locis tantam volumus teneri mensuram ut ex accessu maiorum minores non debeant gravari ne sub tali indulgentia illi qui paucioribus equis uti solebant hactenus plurimam sibi credant potestatem indultam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p33","Canon VIII","If a bishop shall have ordained anyone as a deacon or presbyter without a certain title from which he may receive the necessities of life, let him supply necessities to him until he assigns to him suitable stipends of clerical service in some church.","Episcopus si aliquem sine certo titulo de quo necessaria vitae percipiat in diaconum vel presbyterum ordinaverit tamdiu necessaria ei subministret donec in aliqua ei ecclesia convenientia stipendia militiae clericalis assignet."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p34","Canon VIII","Unless perhaps the person who is ordained shall exist as one who is able to have the sustenance of life from his own or his paternal inheritance.","Nisi forte talis qui ordinatur exstiterit qui de sua vel paterna hereditate subsidium vitae possit habere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p35","Canon IX","A very reprehensible custom has grown up in certain parts that our brothers and fellow bishops or also archdeacons, whom they think will appeal in their cases, bring sentence of suspension or excommunication upon them with no admonition at all having been sent beforehand.","Reprehensibilis valde consuetudo in quibusdam partibus inolevit ut fratres et coepiscopi nostri seu etiam archidiaconi quos appellaturos in causis suis existimant nulla penitus admonitione praemissa suspensionis vel excommunicationis in eos ferant sententiam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p36","Canon IX","Others also, while they dread the sentence and canonical discipline of a superior, interpose an appeal without any burden, and usurp for the defense of iniquity that which is recognized to have been instituted for the aid of the innocent.","Alii etiam dum superioris sententiam et disciplinam canonicam reformidant sine ullo gravamine appellationem obiciunt et ad defensionem iniquitatis usurpant quod ad subsidium innocentium dignoscitur institutum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p37","Canon IX","Wherefore, lest prelates be able to burden subjects without cause or subjects be able under the pretext of appeal to elude the correction of prelates according to their own will, by the present decree we decree that prelates not bring sentence of suspension or excommunication upon subjects unless canonical admonition has been sent beforehand, unless perhaps the fault is such that by its very kind it induces the penalty of excommunication.","Quocirca ne vel praelati valeant sine causa gravare subiectos vel subditi pro sua voluntate sub appellationis obtentu correctionem valeant eludere praelatorum praesenti decreto statuimus ut nec praelati nisi canonica commonitione praemissa suspensionis vel excommunicationis sententiam proferant in subiectos nisi forte talis sit culpa quae ipso genere suo excommunicationis poenam inducat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p38","Canon IX","Nor let subjects burst forth into the voice of appeal before the entry of the cause against ecclesiastical discipline.","Nec subiecti contra disciplinam ecclesiasticam ante ingressum causae in vocem appellationis prorumpant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p39","Canon IX","But if anyone shall have believed that he ought to appeal on account of his necessity, let a suitable term be fixed for him for prosecuting the appeal, within which if perhaps he shall have neglected to prosecute, then let the bishop freely use his authority.","Si vero quisquam pro sua necessitate crediderit appellandum competens ei ad prosequendam appellationem terminus praefigatur infra quem si forte prosequi neglexerit libere tunc episcopus sua auctoritate utatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p40","Canon IX","But if in any negotiation anyone shall have appealed and, the person who was appealed coming, the person who appealed shall have neglected to come, if he had any property of his own, let him make a suitable reimbursement of expenses to him, so that at least terrified by this fear, one may not easily appeal to the burden of another.","Si autem in quocumque negotio aliquis appellaverit et eo qui appellatus fuerit veniente qui appellaverit venire neglexerit si proprium quid habuit competentem ei recompensationem faciat expensarum ut hoc saltem timore perterritus in gravamen alterius non facile quis appellet."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p41","Canon X","Especially in religious places we wish this to be observed, that monks or whatever religious persons, when they are to be corrected for some excess, not presume to appeal against the regular discipline of their prelate and chapter, but humbly and devotedly receive what shall have been usefully enjoined upon them for their salvation.","Praecipue vero in locis religiosis hoc volumus observari ne monachi sive quicumque religiosi cum pro aliquo excessu fuerint corrigendi contra regularem praelati sui et capituli disciplinam appellare praesumant sed humiliter ac devote suscipiant quod pro salute sua utiliter eis fuerit iniunctum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p42","Canon XI","Since in the body of the church all things ought to be treated out of charity and what has been received freely is to be expended freely, it is too horrible that in certain churches venality is reported to have a place, so that something is exacted for bishops or abbots or any ecclesiastical persons to be placed in a see or for presbyters to be introduced into a church, and also for burials and funeral rites of the dead and blessings of those marrying or other sacraments, and that the person who is in need is not able to receive these things unless he shall have been careful to fill the hand of the giver.","Cum in ecclesiae corpore omnia debeant ex caritate tractari et quod gratis receptum est gratis impendi horribile nimis est quod in quibusdam ecclesiis locum venalitas perhibetur habere ita ut pro episcopis vel abbatibus seu quibuscumque personis ecclesiasticis ponendis in sede seu introducendis presbyteris in ecclesiam necnon pro sepulturis et exsequiis mortuorum et benedictionibus nubentium seu aliis sacramentis aliquid exigatur et ille qui indiget non possit ista percipere nisi manum implere curaverit largitoris."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p43","Canon XI","Many think this is permitted to themselves because they judge that the law of custom has prevailed through long usage, not sufficiently attending—because they are blinded by cupidity—that crimes are so much graver the longer they have held the unhappy soul bound.","Putant plures ex hoc sibi licere quia legem moris de longa invaluisse consuetudine arbitrantur non satis quia cupiditate caecati sunt attendentes quod tanto graviora sunt crimina quanto diutius animam infelicem tenuerint alligatam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p44","Canon XI","Lest therefore this be done hereafter, and something be exacted either for ecclesiastical persons to be conducted to a see or for priests to be instituted or for the dead to be buried or also for those marrying to be blessed or also for other sacraments, we more strictly forbid.","Ne igitur hoc de cetero fiat et vel pro personis ecclesiasticis deducendis ad sedem vel sacerdotibus instituendis aut mortuis sepeliendis seu etiam nubentibus benedicendis seu etiam aliis sacramentis aliquid exigatur districtius inhibemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p45","Canon XI","But if anyone shall have presumed to come against this, let him know that he shall have a portion with Gehazi, whose deed he imitates by the base exaction of a gift.","Si quis autem contra hoc venire praesumpserit portionem cum Giezi se noverit habiturum cuius factum turpis muneris exactione imitatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p46","Canon XII","We forbid moreover that new censuses be imposed upon churches by bishops or abbots or other prelates, nor let old ones be increased, nor let them presume to appropriate a portion of the revenues for their own uses, but let the liberties which their maiores desire to be preserved for themselves, let them also preserve for their minors with good will.","Prohibemus insuper ne novi census ab episcopis vel abbatibus aliis ve praelatis imponantur ecclesiis nec veteres augeantur nec partem redituum suis usibus appropriare praesumant sed libertates quas sibi maiores desiderant conservari minoribus quoque suis bona voluntate conservent."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p47","Canon XII","But if anyone shall have acted otherwise, let what he has done be held invalid.","Si quis autem aliter egerit irritum quod fecerit habeatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p48","Canon XIII","Let no ecclesiastical ministries or also benefices or churches be granted or promised to anyone before they are vacant, lest anyone seem to desire the death of a neighbor into whose place and benefice he shall have believed that he will succeed.","Nulla ecclesiastica ministeria seu etiam beneficia vel ecclesiae alicui tribuantur seu promittantur antequam vacent ne desiderare quis mortem proximi videatur in cuius locum et beneficium se crediderit successurum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p49","Canon XIII","For since this is also found prohibited in the laws of the gentiles themselves, it is too shameful and full of the animadversion of divine judgment if the expectation of future succession has a place in the church of God, which even the gentiles themselves have taken care to condemn.","Cum enim id etiam in ipsis gentilium legibus inveniatur prohibitum turpe nimis est et divini plenum animadversione iudicii si locum in dei ecclesia futurae successionis exspectatio habeat quam etiam damnare ipsi gentiles homines curaverunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p50","Canon XIII","But when it shall have happened that ecclesiastical prebends or any offices are vacant in any church, or even if they are vacant now, let them not remain long in suspense, but within six months let them be conferred upon persons who are able to administer worthily.","Cum vero praebendas ecclesiasticas seu quaelibet officia in aliqua ecclesia vacare contigerit vel etiam si modo vacant non diu maneant in suspenso sed infra sex menses personis quae digne administrare valeant conferantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p51","Canon XIII","But if the bishop, where it shall have pertained to him to confer, shall have delayed, let it be done by the chapter.","Si autem episcopus ubi ad eum spectaverit conferre distulerit per capitulum ordinetur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p52","Canon XIII","But if the election shall have pertained to the chapter and it shall not have done this within the aforesaid term, let the bishop carry this out according to God with the counsel of religious men; or if all perhaps shall have neglected, let the metropolitan dispose concerning them according to God without their contradiction.","Quod si ad capitulum electio pertinuerit et infra praedictum terminum hoc non fecerit episcopus hoc secundum deum cum virorum religiosorum consilio exsequatur aut si omnes forte neglexerint metropolitanus de ipsis secundum deum absque illorum contradictione disponat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p53","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","Since we both ought to plant sacred religion and to support what has been planted in every manner, we shall never accomplish this better than if we take care, by the authority committed to us, to nourish what is right and to correct what impedes the progress of truth.","Cum et plantare sacram religionem et plantatam fovere modis omnibus debeamus numquam hoc melius exsequemur quam si nutrire quae recta sunt et corrigere quae profectum veritatis impediunt commissa nobis auctoritate curemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p54","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","But we have learned by the vehement complaint of our brothers and fellow bishops that the brothers of the Temple and of the Hospital and others of religious profession, exceeding the privileges granted to them by the apostolic see, presume many things against episcopal authority which both generate scandal among the people of God and produce grave peril of souls.","Fratrum autem et coepiscoporum nostrorum vehementi conquestione comperimus quod fratres templi et hospitalis alii quoque religiosae professionis indulta sibi ab apostolica sede excedentes privilegia contra episcopalem auctoritatem multa praesumunt quae et scandalum generant in populo dei et grave pariunt periculum animarum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p55","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","For they make it their purpose to receive churches from the hands of laypersons, to admit excommunicated and interdicted persons to ecclesiastical sacraments and burial in their churches without their [the bishops'] knowledge, and to institute and remove priests, and to their brothers going to seek alms—whereas it has been granted to them that in their arrival once a year churches be opened and divine offices be celebrated in them—many of them from one or different houses, coming more often to an interdicted place, abuse the indulgence of privileges in celebrating offices, and then presume to bury the dead at the aforesaid churches.","Proponunt enim quod ecclesias recipiant de manibus laicorum excommunicatos et interdictos ad ecclesiastica sacramenta et sepulturam admittant in ecclesiis suis praeter eorum conscientiam et instituant et amoveant sacerdotes et fratribus eorum ad eleemosynas quaerendas euntibus cum indultum sit eis ut in adventu eorum semel in anno ecclesiae aperiantur atque in eis divina celebrentur officia plures ex eis de una sive diversis domibus ad locum interdictum saepius accedentes indulgentia privilegiorum in celebrandis officiis abutuntur et tunc mortuos apud praedictas ecclesias sepelire praesumunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p56","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","Also, by the occasion of the fraternities which they make in many places, they enervate the strength of episcopal authority, while against their sentence under the pretext of certain privileges they intend to fortify all who are willing to approach and betake themselves to their fraternity.","Occasione quoque fraternitatum quas in pluribus locis faciunt robur episcopalis auctoritatis enervant dum contra eorum sententiam sub aliquorum privilegiorum obtentu munire cunctos intendunt qui ad eorum fraternitatem volunt accedere et se conferre."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p57","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","In these things, because the excess is committed not so much from the knowledge or counsel of maiores as from the indiscretion of certain minors, we have decreed both that the things in which they exceed be removed and that the things which cause doubt be declared.","In his quia non tam de maiorum conscientia vel consilio quam de minorum indiscretione quorundam exceditur et removenda ea in quibus excedunt et quae dubietatem faciunt declaranda decrevimus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p58","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","We forbid both them and any other religious persons whatsoever to receive churches and tithes from the hand of laypersons without the consent of bishops, even those which they have received in recent times against this tenor having been dismissed.","Ecclesias sane et decimas de manu laicorum sine consensu episcoporum tam illos quam quoscumque alios religiosos recipere prohibemus dimissis etiam quas contra tenorem istum moderno tempore receperunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p59","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","We decree that excommunicated and specifically interdicted persons be avoided both by them and by all others according to the sentence of bishops.","Excommunicatos et nominatim interdictos tam ab illis quam ab omnibus aliis iuxta episcoporum sententiam statuimus evitandos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p60","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","In their churches which do not pertain to them in full right, let them present presbyters to be instituted to the bishops, so that they may be responsible to them indeed for the care of the people, but to them [the religious] concerning temporal matters they may render a suitable account.","In ecclesiis suis quae ad eos pleno iure non pertinent instituendos presbyteros episcopis praesentent ut eis quidem de plebis cura respondeant ipsis vero pro rebus temporalibus rationem exhibeant competentem."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p61","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","Let them not dare to remove those instituted without the bishops having been consulted.","Institutos autem episcopis inconsultis non audeant removere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p62","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","But if Templars or Hospitallers shall have come to an interdicted church, let them be admitted to ecclesiastical office only once a year, nor let them bury the bodies of the dead there.","Si vero templarii sive hospitalarii ad ecclesiam interdictam venerint non nisi semel in anno ad ecclesiasticum admittantur officium nec tunc ibi corpora sepeliant defunctorum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p63","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","Concerning fraternities we decree this: that if they shall not have rendered themselves entirely to the aforesaid brothers but shall have chosen to remain in their own properties, let them not on this account be exempted at all from the sentence of bishops, but let them exercise their power over them just as over their other parishioners when they are to be corrected for their excesses.","De fraternitatibus hoc statuimus ut si non se praedictis fratribus omnino reddiderint sed in suis proprietatibus duxerint remanendum propter hoc ab episcoporum sententia nullatenus eximantur sed potestatem suam in eos sicut in alios parochianos suos exerceant cum pro suis excessibus fuerint corrigendi."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p64","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","What has been said concerning the aforesaid brothers, we command to be observed also concerning other religious persons who by their presumption seize the rights of bishops and presume to come against their canonical sentences and the tenor of our privileges.","Quod autem de praedictis fratribus dictum est de aliis quoque religiosis qui praesumptione sua episcoporum iura praeripiunt et contra canonicas eorum sententias et tenorem privilegiorum nostrorum venire praesumunt praecipimus observari."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p65","Segment Two: Canons Xiv–xxvii","But if they shall have come against this institution, let the churches in which they shall have presumed these things be subject to interdict, and let what they have done be held invalid.","Si autem contra hoc institutum venerint et ecclesiae in quibus ista praesumpserint subiaceant interdicto et quod egerint irritum habeatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p66","Canon XV","Let monks not be received into a monastery for a price, let them not be permitted to have private property, let them not be placed singly in villages or towns or in any parochial churches, but let them remain in the greater convent or with some brothers, nor let them, alone among secular persons, await the conflict of spiritual enemies, Solomon saying, \"Woe to the solitary, for if he falls he has no one to lift him up.\"","Monachi non pretio recipiantur in monasterio non peculium permittantur habere non singuli per villas et oppida seu ad quascumque parochiales ponantur ecclesias sed in maiori conventu aut cum aliquibus fratribus maneant nec soli inter saeculares homines spiritualium hostium conflictionem exspectent Salomone dicente vae soli quia si ceciderit non habet sublevantem."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p67","Canon XV","If anyone, having been exacted, shall have given anything for his reception, let him not ascend to sacred orders.","Si quis autem exactus pro sua receptione aliquid dederit ad sacros ordines non ascendat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p68","Canon XV","But he who has received [it], let him be punished with deprivation of his office.","Is autem qui acceperit officii sui privatione mulctetur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p69","Canon XV","But if he shall have had private property, unless it shall have been permitted to him by the abbot for an enjoined administration, let him be removed from the communion of the altar, and he who shall have been found with private property at the end, let neither an oblation be made for him nor let him receive burial among the brothers.","Si vero peculium habuerit nisi ei ab abbate pro iniuncta fuerit administratione permissum a communione removeatur altaris et qui in extremis cum peculio inventus fuerit nec oblatio pro eo fiat nec inter fratres recipiat sepulturam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p70","Canon XV","Which also we command to be observed concerning various religious persons.","Quod etiam de diversis religiosis praecipimus observari."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p71","Canon XV","Moreover, an abbot who shall not have diligently taken care of these things, let him know that he will incur the loss of his office.","Abbas etiam qui ista diligenter non curaverit officii sui iacturam se noverit incursurum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p72","Canon XV","Also, priories or obediences be handed over to no one by the giving of a price; otherwise, both the givers and the receivers shall be made alien from ecclesiastical ministry.","Prioratus quoque sive oboedientiae pretii datione nulli tradantur alioqui et dantes et accipientes a ministerio fiant ecclesiastico alieni."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p73","Canon XV","But priors when they shall have been constituted in conventual churches, let them not be changed except for a manifest and reasonable cause—namely, if they shall have been dilapidators nor shall have lived continently, or shall have done something such that they seem worthy to be removed, or if also for the necessity of a greater office they shall have been transferred by the counsel of the brothers.","Priores vero cum in conventualibus ecclesiis fuerint constituti nisi pro manifesta et rationabili causa non mutentur videlicet si fuerint dilapidatores nec continenter vixerint aut aliquid tale egerint pro quo amovendi merito videantur aut si etiam pro necessitate maioris officii de consilio fratrum fuerint transferendi."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p74","Canon XVI","Clerics constituted in sacred orders who shall have kept their little women in their houses under the mark of incontinence, let them either cast them out and live continently, or let them be made alien from ecclesiastical office and benefice.","Clerici in sacris ordinibus constituti qui mulierculas suas in domibus suis incontinentiae nota tenuerint aut obiciant eas et continenter vivant aut ab officio et beneficio ecclesiastico fiant alieni."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p75","Canon XVI","Whoever shall have been detected to labor under that incontinence which is against nature, on account of which the wrath of God came upon the sons of diffidence and consumed five cities with fire: if they shall have been clerics, let them be cast out from the clergy or be thrust into monasteries to do penance; if laypersons, let them be subjected to excommunication and be made entirely alien from the assembly of the faithful.","Quicumque incontinentia illa quae contra naturam est propter quam venit ira dei in filios diffidentiae et quinque civitates igne consumpsit deprehensi fuerint laborare si clerici fuerint eiciantur a clero vel ad poenitentiam agendam in monasteriis detrudantur si laici excommunicationi subdantur et a coetu fidelium fiant prorsus alieni."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p76","Canon XVII","Moreover, if any cleric shall have presumed to frequent the monasteries of consecrated women without a manifest and necessary cause, let him be restrained by the bishop, and if he shall not have desisted, let him be rendered immune from ecclesiastical benefice.","Monasteria praeterea sanctimonialium si quisquam clericus sine manifesta et necessaria causa frequentare praesumpserit per episcopum arceatur et si non destiterit a beneficio ecclesiastico reddatur immunis."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p77","Canon XVIII","Clerics in subdeaconship and above, and also in minor orders if they are supported by ecclesiastical stipends, let them not presume to become advocates in secular court in negotiations unless they shall have prosecuted their own cause or that of their church, or perhaps for miserable persons who are not able to administer their own causes.","Clerici in subdiaconatu et supra et in minoribus quoque ordinibus si stipendiis ecclesiasticis sustentantur coram iudice saeculari advocati in negotiis fieri non praesumant nisi propriam vel ecclesiae suae causam fuerint prosecuti aut pro miserabilibus forte personis quae proprias causas administrare non possunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p78","Canon XVIII","But let none of the clerics presume to assume the procurations of villages or even secular jurisdictions under any princes or secular men, so that they become their justices.","Sed nec procurationes villarum aut iurisdictiones etiam saeculares sub aliquibus principibus vel saecularibus viris ut iustitiarii eorum fiant clericorum quisquam assumere praesumat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p79","Canon XVIII","If anyone shall have attempted against this, because it is against the doctrine of the apostle saying, \"No one serving God entangles himself in secular affairs,\" and he acts secularly, let him be made alien from ecclesiastical ministry because, the clerical office having been neglected, he immerses himself in the waves of the world in order to please the powerful of the world.","Si quis adversus hoc tentaverit quoniam contra doctrinam apostoli est dicentis nemo militans deo implicat se negotiis saecularibus et saeculariter agit ab ecclesiastico fiat ministerio alienus pro eo quod officio clericali neglecto fluctibus saeculi ut potentibus saeculi placeat se immergit."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p80","Canon XVIII","Moreover, we have decreed that it be more strictly punished if anyone of religious persons shall dare to attempt any of the aforesaid things.","Districtius autem decrevimus puniendum si religiosorum quisquam aliquid praedictorum audeat attentare."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p81","Canon XIX","Because some, not setting a limit to avarice, strive to acquire various ecclesiastical dignities and many parochial churches against the institutions of the sacred canons, so that whereas they scarcely suffice to fulfill one office, they claim for themselves the stipends of very many, we more strictly forbid that this be done hereafter.","Quia nonnulli modum avaritiae non ponentes dignitates diversas ecclesiasticas et plures ecclesias parochiales contra sacrorum canonum instituta nituntur adquirere ita ut cum unum officium vix implere sufficiant stipendia sibi vindicent plurimorum ne id de cetero fiat districtius inhibemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p82","Canon XIX","When therefore a church or ecclesiastical ministry shall have been due to be committed, let such a person be sought who may be able to reside in the place and to exercise its care by himself.","Cum igitur ecclesia vel ecclesiasticum ministerium committi debuerit talis ad hoc persona quaeratur quae residere in loco et curam eius per se ipsum valeat exercere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p83","Canon XIX","But if it shall have been acted otherwise, both let him who received what he received against the sacred canons lose it, and let him who gave be deprived of the power of bestowing.","Quod si aliter fuerit actum et qui receperit quod contra sacros canones accepit amittat et qui dederit largiendi potestate privetur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p84","Canon XIX","Because the ambition of certain persons has now proceeded so far that they are reported to have not two or three but six or more churches, nor can they provide due provision for two, we command by our most beloved brothers and fellow bishops to be corrected, and we wish the neediness of ecclesiastical benefices to be relieved from the multitude which is inimical to the canons—which introduces material of dissolution and vagation and contains certain peril of souls—by those who are able to serve the churches worthily.","Quia in tantum iam quorumdam processit ambitio ut non duas vel tres sed sex aut plures ecclesias perhibeantur habere nec duabus debitam possint provisionem impendere per fratres et coepiscopos nostros carissimos emendari praecipimus et de multitudine canonibus inimica quae dissolutionis materiam et vagationis inducit et certum continet periculum animarum eorum qui ecclesiis digne valeant deservire volumus ecclesiasticis beneficiis indigentiam sublevari."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p85","Canon XX","Moreover, because the audacity of certain laypersons has proceeded so far that, the authority of bishops having been neglected, they institute clerics in churches and remove them also when they wish, and they also distribute possessions and other ecclesiastical goods for the most part according to their own will, and presume to burden both the churches themselves and their men with tolls and exactions, we decree that those who shall have committed these things henceforth be stricken with anathema.","Praeterea quia in tantum quorumdam laicorum processit audacia ut episcoporum auctoritate neglecta clericos instituant in ecclesiis et removeant etiam cum voluerint possessiones quoque atque alia bona ecclesiastica pro sua plerumque voluntate distribuant et tam ecclesias ipsas quam earum homines talliis et exactionibus praesumant gravare eos qui amodo ista commiserint anathemate decernimus feriendos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p86","Canon XX","But a presbyter or cleric who shall have received a church to be held through laypersons without the authority of his own bishop, let him be deprived of communion, and if he shall have persisted, let him be deposed from ecclesiastical ministry and order.","Presbyter autem sive clericus qui ecclesiam per laicos sine proprii episcopi auctoritate receperit tenendam communione privetur et si perstiterit a ministerio ecclesiastico et ordine deponatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p87","Canon XXI","Indeed, because certain laypersons compel ecclesiastical persons and even bishops themselves to stand at their judgment, we decree that those who shall have presumed this hereafter be segregated from the communion of the faithful.","Sane quia laici quidam ecclesiasticas personas et ipsos etiam episcopos suo iudicio stare compellunt eos qui de cetero id praesumpserint a communione fidelium decernimus segregandos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p88","Canon XXI","We also forbid that laypersons, detaining tithes with the peril of their souls, be able to transfer them in any way to other laypersons.","Prohibemus etiam ne laici decimas cum animarum suarum periculo detinentes in alios laicos possint aliquo modo transferre."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p89","Canon XXI","But if anyone shall have received them and shall not have handed them over to the church, let him be deprived of Christian burial.","Si quis vero receperit et ecclesiae non tradiderit christiana sepultura privetur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p90","Canon XXII","Since in the offices of charity we are held bound first to those from whom we acknowledge that we have received a benefit, certain ecclesiastical clerics, when they have perceived many goods from their churches, presume to transfer goods acquired through churches to other uses. This therefore, because it is known to be prohibited also by ancient canons, we likewise forbid.","Cum in officiis caritatis illis primo teneamur obnoxii a quibus nos beneficium cognoscimus accepisse e ecclesiastici quidam clerici cum ab ecclesiis suis multa bona perceperint bona per ecclesias adquisita in alios usus praesumunt transferre hoc igitur quia et antiquis canonibus constat inhibitum nos etiam nihilominus inhibemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p91","Canon XXII","Therefore, willing to provide for the indemnity of churches, whether they shall have died intestate or shall have wished to confer upon others, we command the same goods to remain with the churches.","Indemnitati itaque ecclesiarum providere volentes sive intestati decesserint sive aliis conferre voluerint penes ecclesias eadem bona praecipimus remanere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p92","Canon XXIII","Moreover, because in certain parts certain persons are established for a price who are called deans and exercise episcopal jurisdiction for a certain quantity of money, by the present decree we decree that whoever shall have presumed this hereafter shall be deprived of his office, and the bishop shall lose the power of conferring this office.","Praeterea quoniam quidam in quibusdam partibus sub pretio statuuntur qui decani vocantur et pro certa pecuniae quantitate episcopalem iurisdictionem exercent praesenti decreto statuimus ut qui de cetero id praesumpserit officio suo privetur et episcopus conferendi hoc officium potestatem amittat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p93","Canon XXIV","Since in all churches what shall have seemed [good] to the greater and senior brothers ought to be observed without hesitation, it is too grave and worthy of reproach that the few of certain churches sometimes, not so much from reason as from their own will, often impede the ordination and do not permit ecclesiastical ordination to proceed.","Cum in cunctis ecclesiis quod pluribus et senioribus fratribus visum fuerit incunctanter debeat observari grave nimis et reprehensione est dignum quod quarumdam ecclesiarum pauci quandoque non tam de ratione quam de propria voluntate ordinationem multoties impediunt et ordinationem ecclesiasticam procedere non permittunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p94","Canon XXIV","Wherefore, by the present decree we decree that unless something reasonable shall have been shown by the fewer and inferior, appeal removed, what shall have been established by the greater and senior part of the chapter always prevail and obtain its effect.","Quocirca praesenti decreto statuimus ut nisi a paucioribus et inferioribus aliquid rationabile fuerit ostensum appellatione remota semper praevaleat et suum consequatur effectum quod a maiori et seniori parte capituli fuerit constitutum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p95","Canon XXIV","Nor let our constitution be impeded if perhaps anyone shall say that he is bound by an oath to preserve the custom of his church.","Nec nostram constitutionem impediat si forte aliquis ad conservandam ecclesiae suae consuetudinem iuramento se dicat adstrictum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p96","Canon XXIV","For those are not to be called oaths but rather perjuries which come against the utility of the church and the institutions of the holy fathers.","Non enim dicenda sunt iuramenta sed potius periuria quae contra utilitatem ecclesiasticam et sanctorum patrum veniunt instituta."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p97","Canon XXIV","But if anyone shall have presumed to swear to customs of this kind which are aided neither by reason nor agree with sacred institutions, let him be made alien from the perception of the Lord's body until he shall have done suitable penance.","Si quis autem huiusmodi consuetudines quae nec ratione iuvantur nec sacris congruunt institutis iurare praesumpserit donec congruam egerit poenitentiam a dominici corporis perceptione fiat alienus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p98","Canon XXV","Since in certain places the founders of churches or their heirs abuse the power in which the church has sustained them up to now, and whereas in the church of God there ought to be one person who presides, they themselves strive to choose many without respect for subjection, and whereas one church ought to have one rector, they present many for its defense. Wherefore, by the present decree we decree that if by chance the votes of the founders shall have been divided into many parts, let him be placed over the church who is aided by greater merits and is elected and proved by the assent of the many.","Quoniam in quibusdam locis ecclesiarum fundatores aut heredes eorum potestate in qua eos ecclesia hucusque sustinuit abutuntur et cum in ecclesia dei unus debeat esse qui praesit ipsi plures sine respectu subiectionis eligere moliuntur et cum una ecclesia unius debeat esse rectoris pro sua defensione plurimos repraesentant quocirca praesenti decreto statuimus ut si forte in plures partes fundatorum se vota diffuderint ille praeficiatur ecclesiae qui maioribus iuvatur meritis et plurium eligitur et probatur assensu."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p99","Canon XXV","But if this shall not have been able to be done without scandal, let the bishop ordain the church as he shall have seen better according to God to be ordained.","Si autem hoc sine scandalo fieri nequiverit ordinet antistes ecclesiam sicut melius secundum deum viderit ordinandam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p100","Canon XXV","Let him also do the same if a question concerning the right of patronage shall have emerged between certain persons and to whom it pertains shall not have been defined within three months.","Id ipsum etiam faciat si de iure patronatus quaestio emerserit inter aliquos et cui competat infra tres menses non fuerit definitum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p101","Canon XXVI","Since the church of God, like a pious mother, is held to provide both in those things which pertain to the support of the body and in those things which come for the progress of souls to those in need, lest the opportunity of reading and making progress be withdrawn from the poor who are not able to be aided by the resources of parents, by each cathedral church a suitable benefice shall be assigned to a master who teaches the clerics of the same church and poor scholars for free, by which the necessity of the teacher may be relieved and the way to learning may be opened to the learners.","Quoniam ecclesia dei et in eis quae spectant ad subsidium corporis et in eis quae ad profectum veniunt animarum indigentibus sicut pia mater providere tenetur ne pauperibus qui parentum opibus iuvari non possunt legendi et proficiendi opportunitas subtrahatur per unamquamque ecclesiam cathedralem magistro qui clericos eiusdem ecclesiae et scholares pauperes gratis doceat competens aliquod beneficium assignetur quo docentis necessitas sublevetur et discentibus via pateat ad doctrinam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p102","Canon XXVI","Likewise in other churches or monasteries, if in past times anything shall have been deputed for this purpose, let it be restored.","In aliis quoque restituatur ecclesiis sive monasteriis si retroactis temporibus aliquid in eis ad hoc fuerit deputatum."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p103","Canon XXVI","For the license of teaching, let no one at all exact a price, nor under the pretext of any custom seek anything from those who teach, nor let him forbid anyone who is suitable to teach, license having been sought.","Pro licentia vero docendi nullus omnino pretium exigat vel sub obtentu alicuius consuetudinis ab eis qui docent aliquid quaerat nec docere quempiam expetita licentia qui sit idoneus interdicat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p104","Canon XXVI","But whoever shall have presumed to come against this, let him be made alien from ecclesiastical benefice.","Qui vero contra hoc venire praesumpserit a beneficio ecclesiastico fiat alienus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p105","Canon XXVI","Indeed it seems worthy that in the church of God he not have the fruit of his labor who, by the cupidity of his mind while he sells the license of teaching, strives to impede the progress of churches.","Dignum quidem esse videtur ut in ecclesia dei fructum laboris sui non habeat qui cupiditate animi dum vendit licentiam docendi ecclesiarum profectum nititur impedire."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p106","Canon XXVII","It is recognized as too grave no less for the sin of those who do [it] than for the detriment of those who suffer it that in various parts of the world the rulers and consuls of cities and also others who seem to have power frequently impose many burdens upon so many churches and press them with such heavy and frequent exactions that the priesthood under them appears to have been made of a worse condition than it was under Pharaoh, who did not have knowledge of the divine law.","Non minus pro peccato eorum qui faciunt quam pro illorum detrimento qui sustinent grave nimis esse dignoscitur quod in diversis partibus mundi rectores et consules civitatum necnon et alii qui potestatem habere videntur tot ecclesiis frequenter onera imponunt et ita gravibus eas crebris que exactionibus premunt ut deterioris conditionis factum sub eis sacerdotium videatur quam sub Pharaone fuerit qui divinae legis notitiam non habebat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p107","Canon XXVII","He indeed, all others being subjected to servitude, dismissed his own priests and their possessions in pristine liberty and ministered sustenance to them from the public [treasury].","Ille quidem omnibus aliis servituti subiectis sacerdotes suos et eorum possessiones in pristina libertate dimisit et de publico eis alimoniam ministravit."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p108","Canon XXVII","But these truly impose almost all their own burdens upon churches and afflict them with so many compulsory services that that which Jeremiah laments seems to fit them: \"She who was a prince of provinces has been made under tribute.\"","Isti vero universa fere onera sua imponunt ecclesiis et tot angariis eas affligunt ut illud eis quod Ieremias deplorat competere videatur princeps provinciarum facta est sub tributo."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p109","Canon XXVII","For whether ditches or expeditions or any other things they judge to be done, they wish almost all things to be compiled from the goods of churches, clerics, and the poor of Christ, which are deputed for [their] uses.","Sive quidem fossata sive expeditiones sive quaelibet alia sibi arbitrentur agenda de bonis ecclesiarum clericorum et pauperum Christi usibus deputatis cuncta volunt fere compilari."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p110","Canon XXVII","They also so evacuate the jurisdiction and authority of bishops and other prelates that nothing of power seems to have remained to them in their own men—concerning which it is to be mourned for the churches.","Iurisdictionem etiam et auctoritatem episcoporum et aliorum praelatorum ita evacuant ut nihil potestatis eis in suis videatur hominibus remansisse super quo dolendum est pro ecclesiis."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p111","Canon XXVII","It is also to be mourned nonetheless for those who seem to have utterly cast aside the fear of God and the reverence of the ecclesiastical order.","Dolendum etiam nihilominus et pro ipsis qui timorem dei et ecclesiastici ordinis reverentiam videntur penitus abiecisse."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p112","Canon XXVII","Wherefore, under the constraint of anathema we more severely forbid that they presume to attempt such things hereafter unless the bishop and clergy shall have perceived so great a necessity or utility that they judge that subsidies be conferred through churches without coercion for relieving common necessities when the resources of laypersons do not suffice.","Quocirca sub anathematis districtione severius prohibemus ne de cetero talia praesumant attentare nisi episcopus et clerus tantam necessitatem vel utilitatem aspexerint ut absque coactione ad relevandas communes necessitates ubi laicorum non suppetunt facultates subsidia per ecclesias existiment conferenda."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p113","Canon XXVII","But if consuls or others shall have presumed this hereafter and, having been admonished, perhaps shall have been unwilling to desist, let both they themselves and their supporters know that they lie under excommunication, nor let them be restored to the communion of the faithful unless they shall have made suitable satisfaction.","Si autem consules aut alii de cetero id praesumpserint et commoniti desistere forte noluerint tam ipsi quam eorum fautores excommunicationi se noverint subiacere nec communioni fidelium reddantur nisi satisfactionem fecerint competentem."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p114","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","Following in the footsteps of our predecessors, popes of happy memory Innocent and Eugenius, we forbid the detestable markets or fairs which are commonly called tournaments to be held, in which soldiers are accustomed to come by agreement and to contend rashly for the display of their strength and their audacity, from which deaths of men and perils of souls often arise.","Felicis memoriae papae Innocentii et Eugenii praedecessorum nostrorum vestigiis inhaerentes detestabiles nundinas vel ferias quas vulgo torneamenta vocant in quibus milites ex condicto venire solent et ad ostentationem virium suarum et audaciae temerarie congrediuntur unde mortes hominum et animarum pericula saepe proveniunt fieri prohibemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p115","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","But if anyone of them shall have died there, although pardon be not denied to him seeking it, let him nevertheless lack ecclesiastical burial.","Quod si quis eorum ibidem mortuus fuerit quamvis ei poscenti venia non negetur ecclesiastica tamen careat sepultura."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p116","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","We command that the truces be observed inviolably by all from Wednesday after sunset until Monday at sunrise, and from the advent of the Lord until the octave of Epiphany, and from Septuagesima until the octave of Easter.","Treugas a quarta feria post occasum solis usque ad secundam feriam in ortum solis et ab adventu domini usque ad octavas epiphaniae et a septuagesima usque ad octavas paschae ab omnibus inviolabiliter observari praecipimus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p117","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","But if anyone shall have attempted to break the truce, after the third admonition if he shall not have made satisfaction, let his bishop pronounce sentence of excommunication and let him announce it in writing to the neighboring bishops.","Si quis autem treugam frangere tentaverit post tertiam commonitionem si non satisfecerit episcopus suus sententiam excommunicationis dictet et scriptam vicinis episcopis annuntiet."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p118","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","Moreover, let no bishop receive an excommunicated person into communion; rather, let each confirm the sentence received in writing.","Episcopus autem nullus excommunicatum in communionem suscipiat immo scripto susceptam sententiam quisque confirmet."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p119","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","But if anyone shall have presumed to violate this, let him be subject to the peril of his order; and since a threefold cord is not easily broken, we command that bishops, having regard only to God and the salvation of the people, all tepidity having been set aside, provide mutual counsel and aid to one another for firmly keeping the peace, nor let them omit this on account of anyone's love or hatred.","Si quis autem hoc violare praesumpserit ordinis sui periculo subiaceat et quoniam funiculus triplex non facile rumpitur praecipimus ut episcopi solum dei et salutis populi habentes respectum omni tepiditate seposita ad pacem firmiter tenendam mutuum sibi consilium et auxilium praestent neque hoc alicuius amore vel odio praetermittant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p120","Concerning Tournaments and the Truce of God","But if anyone shall have been found tepid in the work of God, let him incur the loss of his dignity.","Quod si quis in opere dei tepidus fuerit inventus damnum dignitatis suae incurrat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p121","Concerning Safe Conduct","We renew that presbyters, monks, clerics, conversi, pilgrims, merchants, peasants going and returning, and those existing in agriculture, and the animals which carry seed to the field, may rejoice in fitting security, nor let anyone presume rashly in any way to establish new exactions of tolls without the authority and consent of kings and princes, or to hold established ones anew, or to increase old ones.","Innovamus ut presbyteri monachi clerici conversi peregrini mercatores rustici euntes et redeuntes et in agricultura exsistentes et animalia quae semina portant ad agrum congrua securitate laetentur nec quisquam alicui novas pedagiorum exactiones sine auctoritate regum et principum consensu statuere aut statutas de novo tenere aut veteres augmentare aliquo modo temere praesumat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p122","Concerning Safe Conduct","But if anyone shall have presumed to come against this and, having been admonished, shall not have desisted, let him lack Christian communion until he makes satisfaction.","Si quis autem contra hoc venire praesumpserit et commonitus non destiterit donec satisfaciat communione careat christiana."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p123","Concerning Lepers","Since the apostle says that more abundant honor is to be bestowed upon the weaker members, certain ecclesiastical [persons], seeking their own things and not those of Jesus Christ, do not permit lepers, who are not able to dwell with the healthy nor to gather with others to church, to have churches and cemeteries nor to be aided by the ministry of their own priest.","Cum dicat apostolus abundantiorem honorem membris infirmioribus deferendum ecclesiastici quidam quae sua sunt non quae Iesu Christi quaerentes leprosis qui cum sanis habitare non possunt et ad ecclesiam cum aliis convenire ecclesias et coemeteria non permittunt habere nec proprii iuvari ministerio sacerdotis."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p124","Concerning Lepers","Because this is recognized to be far from Christian piety, we constitute by apostolic benignity that wherever so many at once shall have been gathered together in common life that they are able to constitute a church for themselves with a cemetery and to enjoy their own presbyter, they be permitted to have [these] without any contradiction.","Quod quia procul a pietate christiana esse dignoscitur de benignitate apostolica constituimus ut ubicumque tot simul sub communi vita fuerint congregati qui ecclesiam sibi cum coemeterio constituere et proprio gaudere valeant presbytero sine contradictione aliqua permittantur habere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p125","Concerning Lepers","Let them be careful, however, that they by no means exist as injurious to older churches concerning parochial right.","Caveant tamen ut iniuriosi veteribus ecclesiis de iure parochiali nequaquam exsistant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p126","Concerning Lepers","For what is granted to them for the sake of piety we are unwilling to redound to the injury of others.","Quod namque eis pro pietate conceditur ad aliorum iniuriam nolumus redundare."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p127","Concerning Lepers","We also decree that they not be compelled to pay tithes concerning gardens and the nurture of their animals.","Statuimus etiam ut de hortis et nutrimentis animalium suorum decimas tribuere non cogantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p128","Concerning Saracens","Savage cupidity has so occupied the minds of certain persons that, although they glory in the Christian name, they bear arms, iron, and timbers of helmets to the Saracens, and they become equal to them or even superior in malice while they supply arms and necessities to them for attacking Christians.","Ita quorumdam animos occupavit saeva cupiditas ut cum glorientur nomine christiano Sarracenis arma ferrum et lignamina galearum deferant et pares eis aut etiam superiores in malitia fiant dum ad impugnandos christianos arma eis et necessaria subministrant."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p129","Concerning Saracens","There are also those who for their own cupidity exercise the command and care of steering in the galleys and piratical ships of the Saracens.","Sunt etiam qui pro sua cupiditate in galeis et piraticis Sarracenorum navibus regimen et curam gubernationis exercent."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p130","Concerning Saracens","Such therefore we judge to be cut off from the communion of the church and subject to excommunication on account of their iniquity, and to be punished with the deprivation of their goods by the secular princes and consuls of cities, and if they shall have been captured, to become the slaves of those capturing [them].","Tales igitur a communione ecclesiae praecisos et excommunicationi pro sua iniquitate subiectos et rerum suarum per saeculi principes catholicos et consules civitatum privatione mulctari et capientium servos si capti fuerint fore censemus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p131","Concerning Saracens","We also command that frequent and solemn excommunication be pronounced against them in the churches of maritime cities.","Praecipimus etiam ut per ecclesias maritimarum urbium crebra et solemnis excommunicatio proferatur in eos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p132","Concerning Saracens","Let those also be subjected to the penalty of excommunication who presume to capture Romans or other Christians sailing by ship for the sake of trade or other honest causes, or to despoil them of their goods.","Excommunicationis quoque poenae subdantur qui Romanos aut alios christianos pro negotiatione vel aliis causis honestis navigio vectos aut capere aut rebus suis spoliare praesumunt."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p133","Concerning Saracens","Those also who, with damnable cupidity, presume to despoil of their goods Christians suffering shipwreck—whom according to the rule of faith they are held to aid—unless they shall have restored what was taken away, let them know that they lie under excommunication.","Illi etiam qui christianos naufragia patientes quibus secundum regulam fidei auxilio esse tenentur damnanda cupiditate rebus suis spoliare praesumunt nisi ablata reddiderint excommunicationi se noverint subiacere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p134","Concerning Usurers","Because in almost all places the crime of usury has so grown up that many, other businesses having been neglected, exercise usuries as if lawfully, and do not at all attend to how they are condemned by the page of both Testaments, therefore we constitute that manifest usurers be neither admitted to the communion of the altar nor, if they shall have died in this sin, receive Christian burial; nor let anyone receive their oblation.","Quia in omnibus fere locis crimen usurarum ita inolevit ut multi aliis negotiis praetermissis quasi licite usuras exerceant et qualiter utriusque testamenti pagina condemnentur nequaquam attendant ideo constituimus ut usurarii manifesti nec ad communionem admittantur altaris nec christianam si in hoc peccato decesserint accipiant sepulturam sed nec eorum oblationem quisquam accipiat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p135","Concerning Usurers","But he who shall have received [it] or shall have handed them over to Christian burial, let him also be compelled to restore what he received, and let him remain suspended from the execution of his office until he makes satisfaction at the discretion of his bishop.","Qui autem acceperit aut eos christianae tradiderit sepulturae et ea quae acceperit reddere compellatur et donec ad arbitrium sui episcopi satisfaciat ab officii sui maneat exsecutione suspensus."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p136","Concerning Jews and Saracens","Jews or Saracens be not permitted to have Christian servants in their houses, neither under the pretext of nourishing children nor for service nor any other cause.","Iudaei sive Sarraceni nec sub alendorum puerorum obtentu nec pro servitio nec alia qualibet causa christiana mancipia in domibus suis permittantur habere."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p137","Concerning Jews and Saracens","Moreover, let those be excommunicated who presume to dwell with them.","Excommunicentur autem qui cum eis praesumpserint habitare."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p138","Concerning Jews and Saracens","We also decree that the testimony of Christians against Jews in all cases be received, since they use their own witnesses against Christians, and we decree that whoever shall have wished to prefer Jews to Christians in this part be stricken with anathema, since it is fitting that Jews be subject to Christians and be supported by them for the sake of humanity alone.","Testimonium quoque christianorum adversus Iudaeos in omnibus causis cum illi adversus christianos testibus suis utantur recipiendum esse censemus et anathemate decernimus feriendos quicumque Iudaeos christianis voluerint in hac parte praeferre cum eos subiacere christianis oporteat et ab eis pro sola humanitate foveri."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p139","Concerning the Conversion of Jews","Moreover, if any, God inspiring, shall have been converted to the Christian faith, let them by no means be excluded from their possessions, since it is fitting that those converted to the faith be of a better condition than they were held to be before they received the faith.","Si qui praeterea deo inspirante ad fidem se converterint christianam a possessionibus suis nullatenus excludantur cum melioris conditionis conversos ad fidem esse oporteat quam antequam fidem acceperunt habebantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p140","Concerning the Conversion of Jews","But if it shall have been done otherwise, we enjoin upon the princes or powers of those same places under penalty of excommunication that they cause the portion of their inheritance and goods to be exhibited to them from the whole.","Si autem secus factum fuerit principibus vel potestatibus eorumdem locorum sub poena excommunicationis iniungimus ut portionem hereditatis et bonorum suorum ex integro eis faciant exhiberi."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p141","Concerning Heretics","Just as blessed Leo says, although ecclesiastical discipline, content with priestly judgment, does not effect bloody vengeances, it is nevertheless aided by the constitutions of catholic princes, so that men often seek a salutary remedy while they fear that bodily punishment may befall them.","Sicut ait beatus Leo licet ecclesiastica disciplina sacerdotali contenta iudicio cruentas non efficiat ultiones catholicorum tamen principum constitutionibus adiuvatur ut saepe quaerant homines salutare remedium dum corporale super se metuunt evenire supplicium."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p142","Concerning Heretics","Therefore, because in Gascony, the Albigensian region, and the parts of Toulouse, and in other places, the damned perversity of heretics—whom some call Cathars, others Patrines, others Publicans, others by other names—has so grown up that they now exercise their wickedness not in secret as some do, but publicly manifest their error and attract the simple and the weak to their consent, we decree that they and their defenders and receivers be subject to anathema, and under anathema we forbid that anyone presume to hold or support them in his houses or land or to exercise trade with them.","Eapropter quia in Gasconia Albigesio et partibus Tolosanis et aliis locis ita haereticorum quos alii catharos alii Patrinos alii publicanos alii aliis nominibus vocant invaluit damnata perversitas ut iam non in occulto sicut aliqui nequitiam suam exerceant sed suum errorem publice manifestent et ad suum consensum simplices attrahant et infirmos eos et defensores eorum et receptores anathemati decernimus subiacere et sub anathemate prohibemus ne quis eos in domibus vel in terra sua tenere vel fovere vel negotiationem cum eis exercere praesumat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p143","Concerning Heretics","But if they shall have died in this sin, under the pretext of any of our privileges granted to anyone nor under any other occasion, let neither an oblation be made for them nor let them receive burial among Christians.","Si autem in hoc peccato decesserint non sub nostrorum privilegiorum cuilibet indultorum obtentu nec sub aliacumque occasione aut oblatio fiat pro eis aut inter christianos recipiant sepulturam."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p144","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","Concerning the Brabantians, Aragonians, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaverdini, who exercise such great savagery against Christians that they show deference neither to churches nor to monasteries, nor spare widows and orphans, nor the aged and the young, nor any age or sex, but after the manner of pagans destroy and lay waste all things, we similarly constitute that those who shall have hired them or held or supported them, in the regions in which they so rage, be publicly denounced in churches on Lord's days and other solemn days, and be held bound by the same entirely sentence and penalty as the aforesaid heretics, nor let them be received into the communion of the church unless, that pestiferous society and heresy having been abjured.","De Brabantionibus et Aragonensibus Navarriis Basculis Coterellis et Triaverdinis qui tantam in christianos immanitatem exercent ut nec ecclesiis nec monasteriis deferant non viduis et pupillis non senibus et pueris nec cuilibet parcant aetati aut sexui sed more paganorum omnia perdant et vastent similiter constituimus ut qui eos conduxerint vel tenuerint vel foverint per regiones in quibus taliter debacchantur in dominicis et aliis solemnibus diebus per ecclesias publice denuntientur et eadem omnino sententia et poena cum praedictis haereticis habeantur adstricti nec ad communionem recipiantur ecclesiae nisi societate illa pestifera et haeresi abiuratis."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p145","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","Moreover, let those know themselves to be released from the bond of fidelity and homage and of all service—whoever shall have been bound to them by any pact—as long as they shall have remained in such great iniquity.","Relaxatos autem se noverint a debito fidelitatis et hominii ac totius obsequii donec in tanta iniquitate permanserint quicumque illis aliquo pacto tenentur annexi."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p146","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","We enjoin upon all the faithful moreover for the remission of sins that they oppose themselves manfully to such great calamities and defend the Christian people with arms against them.","Ipsis autem cunctis que fidelibus in remissionem peccatorum iniungimus ut tantis cladibus se viriliter opponant et contra eos armis populum christianum tueantur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p147","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","Let their goods also be confiscated, and let it be free for princes to subject such men to servitude.","Confiscentur que eorum bona et liberum sit principibus huiusmodi homines subicere servituti."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p148","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","Those who shall have died there in true penance, let them not doubt that they shall receive both the indulgence of sins and the fruit of eternal reward.","Qui autem in vera poenitentia ibi decesserint et peccatorum indulgentiam et fructum mercedis aeternae se non dubitent percepturos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p149","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","We also, trusting in the mercy of God and the authority of the blessed apostles Peter and Paul, to the faithful Christians who shall have taken up arms against them and, at the counsel of bishops or other prelates, shall have striven to expel them, relax two years of the penance enjoined; or if they shall have had a longer stay there, we commit to the discretion of the bishops to whom the care of this matter shall have been enjoined, that according to the measure of labor greater indulgence be granted to them at their arbitration.","Nos etiam de misericordia dei et beatorum apostolorum Petri et Pauli auctoritate confisi fidelibus christianis qui contra eos arma susceperint et ad episcoporum seu aliorum praelatorum consilium ad eos certaverint expugnandos biennium de poenitentia iniuncta relaxamus aut si longiorem ibi moram habuerint episcoporum discretioni quibus huius rei cura fuerit iniuncta committimus ut ad eorum arbitrium secundum modum laboris maior eis indulgentia tribuatur."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p150","Concerning Brabançons, Aragonese, Navarrese, Basques, Coterelli, and Triaderdini","Those moreover who shall have despised to obey the admonition of bishops in this matter, we command to be made alien from the perception of the Lord's body and blood.","Illos autem qui admonitioni episcoporum in huiusmodi parte parere contempserint a perceptione corporis et sanguinis domini iubemus fieri alienos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p151","Concerning the Protection of Those Fighting Against Heretics","In the meantime, those who, with the ardor of faith, shall have assumed this labor for expelling them, just as those who visit the Lord's sepulcher, we receive under the defense of the church and we decree to remain secure from all disturbances both in goods and in persons.","Interim vero eos qui ardore fidei ad eos expugnandum laborem istum assumpserint sicut eos qui sepulchrum dominicum visitant sub ecclesiae defensione recipimus et ab universis inquietationibus tam in rebus quam in personis statuimus manere securos."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p152","Concerning the Protection of Those Fighting Against Heretics","But if any of you shall have presumed to molest them, let him be stricken with the sentence of excommunication by the bishop of the place, and let the sentence be observed by all until both what has been taken away be restored and satisfaction be suitably made for the losses inflicted.","Si vero quispiam vestrum praesumpserit eos molestare per episcopum loci excommunicationis sententia feriatur et tamdiu sententia servetur ab omnibus donec et ablata reddantur et de illatis damnis congrue iterum satisfaciat."],["vol2/lateran-iii/index.html","p153","Concerning the Protection of Those Fighting Against Heretics","Moreover, bishops or presbyters who shall not have resisted such persons strongly, let them be punished with deprivation of their office until they obtain the mercy of the apostolic see.","Episcopi vero sive presbyteri qui talibus fortiter non restiterint officii sui privatione mulctentur donec misericordiam apostolicae sedis obtineant."]];